<DocsLayout
  title="Sidecar"
  subtitle="The Bun process that owns SQLite, HTTP, plugins, and the assistant host."
  description="CADCAMFUN sidecar: process model, handlers, repositories, configuration, and what is still missing."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="status" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      WP4 on the task board is <strong>in progress</strong>. Every contract group is served
      (plugins, auth, analytics, waitlist, and files were added). Families without a contract
      are still missing. See <code>specs/11-api-parity-brief.md</code>. Owner directory:
      <code>apps/sidecar</code> (<code>@cadcamfun/sidecar</code>). Spec:
      <code>specs/05-api-sidecar.md</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="note" title="About 15% of legacy route files">
      <p>
        Spec 05 records projects, materials, tools, machine configs, drawings, components,
        toolpaths, library, health, and native system routes as implemented end to end, plus
        production costs, organizations, notifications, legacy plugin routes, files, analytics,
        waitlist, and seven auth routes, each with HTTP tests. That is still a minority of the
        195 legacy route files. Contract coverage and handler coverage are different numbers.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="process" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Process</h2>
    <p>
      Tauri spawns the compiled binary. The sidecar binds <code>127.0.0.1</code> only, on port
      <code>0</code> so the OS assigns a port. After migrations succeed and the server is
      listening it prints one JSON line and nothing else on that channel.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="text" title="Stdout">
{`{"event":"ready","port":53211}
{"event":"error","message":"…"}`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      The shell passes <code>CADCAMFUN_TOKEN</code> (32 random bytes, new every launch) and
      reads the port. The webview sends <code>Authorization: Bearer</code>. CORS allows
      <code>tauri://localhost</code>, <code>http://tauri.localhost</code>, and the Vite origin in
      dev builds. Stdin close and <code>SIGTERM</code> shut the process down: finish requests,
      checkpoint SQLite, close the handle in the layer finaliser. Spec 07 sends
      <code>&#123;"event":"shutdown"&#125;</code> on stdin and waits up to 2 seconds.
      <code>apps/sidecar/test/process.test.ts</code> covers three real-process modes. Driving that
      drain through the Rust shell with the compiled binary is still an ignored test.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="layout" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Layout</h2>
    <p>Directories under <code>apps/sidecar/src</code>:</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Path</th><th>Role</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>main.ts</code></td><td>Build the layer graph, print the ready line, <code>Layer.launch</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>config.ts</code></td><td>The only module that reads process configuration. Exposes <code>cadcamfun/AppConfig</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>layers.ts</code></td><td>App layer composition.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>startup.ts</code>, <code>shutdown.ts</code>, <code>observability.ts</code></td><td>Boot order, finalisers, log records.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>http/</code></td><td>One handler file per group: <code>HttpApiBuilder.group</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>repos/</code></td><td>The only place that calls <code>Database.query</code>. JSON columns are decoded here.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>services/</code></td><td>Domain services: AI, costs, storage, VCS, workflows, payments, companion gateway.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>plugins/</code></td><td><code>host.ts</code>, <code>repo.ts</code>, <code>bootstrap-script.ts</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data/</code></td><td>Seed or fixture data used by the server.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Handler files match the contract groups:
      <code>projects.ts</code>, <code>drawings.ts</code>, <code>components.ts</code>,
      <code>toolpaths.ts</code>, <code>toolpath-generator.ts</code>, <code>materials.ts</code>,
      <code>tools.ts</code>, <code>machine-configs.ts</code>, <code>library.ts</code>,
      <code>files.ts</code>, <code>ai.ts</code>, <code>plugins.ts</code>, <code>auth.ts</code>,
      <code>analytics.ts</code>, <code>billing.ts</code>, <code>organizations.ts</code>,
      <code>notifications.ts</code>, <code>waitlist.ts</code>, <code>production-costs.ts</code>,
      <code>vcs.ts</code>, <code>companion.ts</code>, <code>kv.ts</code>, <code>health.ts</code>,
      and the storage twins <code>materials-storage.ts</code>, <code>tools-storage.ts</code>,
      <code>machine-configs-storage.ts</code>. There is no <code>http/cam-setup.ts</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Repositories include <code>project-repo.ts</code>, <code>drawing-repo.ts</code>,
      <code>toolpath-repo.ts</code>, <code>project-vcs-repo.ts</code>,
      <code>plugin-registry-repo.ts</code>, and one file per aggregate. Each repository test uses
      <code>Database.layer(&#123; path: ":memory:", migrationsFolder &#125;)</code>. HTTP tests use
      an in-process web handler (<code>51_http-server/20_testing.ts</code> in the Effect docs).
    </p>
    <p>
      On first start <code>LocalProfile</code> ensures one <code>User</code> row and exposes its
      id as <code>ownerId</code>. <code>KvStore</code> (<code>services/kv.ts</code>) persists
      JSON-compatible AI context and preferences. <code>CamProgramDocument</code> validation for
      native saves lives with the toolpath handlers: the sidecar reruns a captured kernel
      request before it accepts native evidence.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="config" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Configuration</h2>
    <p>
      Read once in <code>config.ts</code>. Other modules take <code>AppConfig</code>. AI model
      keys are not environment variables. The UI pushes them with <code>PUT /ai/credentials</code>.
      They are also stored at <code>&lt;data dir&gt;/ai/credentials.json</code>, owner-only.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Role</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_TOKEN</code></td><td>Required. Per-launch bearer token.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_DATA_DIR</code></td><td>Required. Database at <code>&lt;dir&gt;/cadcamfun.db</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_MIGRATIONS_DIR</code></td><td>Bundled <code>drizzle/</code> SQL.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_LOG_LEVEL</code></td><td>Effect log level.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_APP_URL</code></td><td>Optional base for email links.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_DEBUG_LINKS</code></td><td>Echo reset and magic links in the response. There is no mail transport yet.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CADCAMFUN_AI_OFFLINE</code></td><td>Tests set this so the models.dev seed does not block boot.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code>, <code>STRIPE_PRICE_BASIC|PRO|ENTERPRISE</code></td><td>Optional. Missing key means checkout answers unconfigured.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Auth link JWTs use a per-install secret at <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/auth-secret</code>.
      Revoked session ids live in <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/auth-revoked.json</code> until they
      expire. Plugin files for the legacy installer live under
      <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/storage/plugins/&lt;id&gt;/</code>. The companion certificate lives
      under <code>&lt;dataDir&gt;/companion/</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Build the host binary with <code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/sidecar build</code>. CI uses
      <code>build:all</code> for macOS arm64 and x64, Windows x64, and Linux x64. The outfile
      pattern is <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/binaries/sidecar-&lt;target-triple&gt;</code>.
      Effect log lines on stderr are one JSON object per event. Rust keeps the <code>level</code>
      field and redacts bearer tokens before it publishes the line.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="served" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What is served</h2>
    <p>
      Use this list when you are wiring a screen. A route outside it needs a contract file, a
      handler, a repository, and an HTTP test before a UI should call it.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Projects, drawings, components, toolpaths (generate, G-code, verify), materials, tools, machine configs, library.</li>
      <li>Legacy <code>GET /api/health</code> and authenticated <code>GET /health</code>, <code>GET /version</code>.</li>
      <li>Production costs, organizations, notifications, files, analytics (<code>system-metrics</code>, <code>track</code>), waitlist.</li>
      <li>Seven contract-covered auth routes, session revoke on sign-out, magic-link and reset consumption.</li>
      <li>Legacy <code>/api/plugins/*</code> (zip install, bootstrap script). The SDK worker host is a separate surface and is not the HTTP group. See <a href="/docs/plugins">Plugins</a>.</li>
      <li>AI chat stream, credentials, models, stateless advice endpoints, and VCS tools used by the assistant.</li>
      <li>Companion gateway on a separate HTTPS port when Settings turns it on.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <code>PaymentProvider</code> creates Stripe checkout and portal sessions when a secret is
      configured. Webhook handling stores plan and customer ids. Open question 3 in spec 00 is
      decided: Stripe, optional, no license-key product.
    </p>
    <p>
      Runtime startup does not prewarm the AI SDK or download model metadata. The first catalogue
      access owns that request. Scope shutdown aborts it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Handlers must not open SQLite themselves. They call a repository, and the repository calls <code>Database.query</code>.</li>
      <li>Modules other than <code>config.ts</code> must not read <code>process.env</code>.</li>
      <li>The sidecar must not listen on a public interface for the main API. <code>127.0.0.1</code> only. The companion gateway is the opt-in exception, and it has its own token and route allow-list.</li>
      <li>The per-launch bearer token must not be written to disk or to logs.</li>
      <li>Adding a contract group in <code>packages/api</code> does not implement a route. The handler and the HTTP test do.</li>
      <li>Geometry algorithms stay in <code>packages/core</code>. The sidecar calls them. It does not reimplement offset or posting.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section id="ready" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Ready event</h2>
    <p>
      Entry is <code>bun src/main.ts</code> (<code>apps/sidecar/src/main.ts</code>). After
      <code>/api/health</code> succeeds, stdout is one JSON object
      <code>&#123; event: "ready", port &#125;</code>. Failure is
      <code>&#123; event: "error", message &#125;</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

